$ signet link --help
-- stdout --
Links the wallet you deploy contracts from to your Signet handle.

signet prints a URL to approve in your browser. Approving it proves you own
the handle; signing a challenge with your local identity proves you control
the deploy key. Both are required, and signet never reads your secret key —
signing goes through the stellar CLI.

The profile shows the wallet's contracts once Signet's indexer has scanned
it. --wait keeps signet running until then (5m by default, or
--wait=<duration>) and prints what it found; running out of time is not an
error. signet status shows the same progress later.

Usage:
  signet link [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help                 help for link
      --no-browser           print the approval URL instead of opening a browser
      --wait duration[=5m]   after linking, wait up to this long for the indexer to scan the wallet (--wait alone: 5m)

Global Flags:
      --context string         deployment context to use (overrides SIGNET_CONTEXT and the config file's current context)
      --insecure               allow a plain-http deployment URL on a non-local host (signed challenges travel in cleartext; use only against a deployment you control)
      --json                   write a single JSON result to stdout instead of human-readable output (diagnostics go to stderr)
      --network string         Stellar network to talk to (overrides SIGNET_NETWORK, the context, and default "testnet")
      --sign-with-key string   identity to sign with, for non-interactive use (same value as STELLAR_SIGN_WITH_KEY; not remembered)
      --source string          identity to sign as (remembered in the config file for next time)
      --url string             Signet deployment URL (overrides SIGNET_URL, the config file, and the default)
-- stderr --
(empty)
-- exit 0 --
